#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189179} :activity/id #uuid "831069d2-736b-52d1-a2bb-6631187686b5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049908 :topic/id #uuid "1dc40382-49d1-5d5b-a59d-1be47c4f903d" :topic/math-academy-id 3929} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189179 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189404 :tutorial/content "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, where the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is given by $\\mu_{X \\mid y}$. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\begin{bmatrix}X\\, & \\,Y=y\\end{bmatrix} = \\mu_{X \\mid y}\n$$\n\nThe **conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\begin{bmatrix}X\\, & \\,Y\\end{bmatrix} = \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}(X - \\mu_{X \\mid y} \\big)^2 \\, & \\, Y=y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs with the discrete case, this definition can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid y}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X^2 \\, & \\, Y=y \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nand $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$. Note that these formulas are analogous to those for $\\textrm{Var}[X]$ for continuous $X$.\n\nWhen we select a particular value of $y$, the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ returns a real number. However, if $y$ is not specified, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm {Var}\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives us a *function* of $y$.\n\nWe have an analogous definition for the **conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x{:}$**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\mu_{Y \\mid x} = \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix}$ is the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$,\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\displaystyle \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y$, and\n- $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$." :tutorial/id #uuid "cc60678b-fd8c-537f-99be-cee66503c859" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6444 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "90a5c594-6537-5336-90c2-6eca3c31d58b" :step/math-academy-id 38946 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189203}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189180 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188043 :question/id #uuid "ea6a79c4-09fc-5ae9-9e92-e7bacd4939d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10340"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049871} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050965}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188655} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188721}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"} :step/id #uuid "53d73871-be25-53a5-8455-4cf04e078787" :step/math-academy-id 38947 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189181}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189181 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188044 :question/id #uuid "fef21fcb-bab6-5f33-a792-280e28a97f81" :question/math-academy-id "e-10341"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188722} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188724}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"} :step/id #uuid "7bbe5d6f-436a-56b7-b6c3-4b50cf86ea46" :step/math-academy-id 38948 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189182}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189182 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188045 :question/id #uuid "acb4923c-ce04-5cd5-af01-2f078a18ceed" :question/math-academy-id "e-10342"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188719}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"} :step/id #uuid "e3ab0323-0d1c-5360-8b97-deeb42c28a59" :step/math-academy-id 38949} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189203 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189410 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables. It is known that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{4y^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nand that\n\n$$\n\\mu_{Y \\mid 1}=\\dfrac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nWhat is the conditional variance\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=1\\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y^{2} \\cdot 4y^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}4y^{5}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{2y^{6}}{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} - (\\frac{4}{5})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{16}{25} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{75}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "51fd1dbf-d36f-5e8c-b62b-ede292dae6da" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6490 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "0112f403-404f-5282-8492-4ad12782a53c" :step/math-academy-id 39321 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189180}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186188512}]}
